                <pb facs="0180" n="172" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg172"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.008 North Pacific/282b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-07T18:00:00-05:00">February 7, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. Because of situation outlined in Department’s 39, February 4, 6 p.m., it
                    would greatly contribute to desired purpose and we would be relieved of possible
                    embarrassment if an early reply to your representations could be obtained from
                    the Japanese Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
